.ds q \N'34'
.TH litecompmgr 1
.SH NAME
litecompmgr \- a lightweight compositor for X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B litecompmgr [\-d display] [\-r radius] [\-o opacity] [\-l left-offset] [\-t top-offset] [\-i opacity] [\-e opacity] [\-R radius] [\-cCfFS]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B litecompmgr
is a lightweight compositor for X11, forked from fastcompmgr 0.6.1 (which
is based on Dana Jansens' version of xcompmgr and on an early version of
Christopher Jeffrey's compton). It restores working window fading (including
fade-out of the last window contents), adds anti-aliased rounded corners,
and reduces per-frame compositing overhead, while keeping the win\-dow frame
opacity, inactive window transparency and shadows on argb windows of its
ancestors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d\ display
Specifies the display to manage.
.TP
.BI \-r\ radius
Specifies the blur radius for client-side shadows.
.TP
.BI \-o\ opacity
Specifies the opacity for client-side shadows.
.TP
.BI \-l\ left-offset
Specifies the left offset for client-side shadows.
.TP
.BI \-t\ top-offset
Specifies the top offset for client-side shadows.
.TP
.BI \-I\ fade-in-step
Specifies the opacity change between steps while fading in.
.TP
.BI \-O\ fade-out-step
Specifies the opacity change between steps while fading out.
.TP
.BI \-D\ fade-delta
Specifies the time (in milliseconds) between steps in a fade.
.TP
.BI \-c
Enable client-side shadows on windows.
.TP
.BI \-f
When \-c is specified, enables a smooth fade effect for transient windows like
menus, and for all windows on hide and restore events.
.TP
.BI \-C
When \-c is specified, attempts to avoid painting shadows on panels and docks.
.TP
.BI \-F
When \-f is specified, also enables the fade effect when windows change their
opacity, as with transset(1).
.TP
.BI \-i\ opacity
Specifies inactive window transparency. (0.1 - 1.0)
.TP
.BI \-e\ opacity
Specifies window frame transparency. (0.1 - 1.0)
.TP
.BI \-R\ radius
Specifies the corner radius for anti-aliased rounded corners. (default 8, 0 disables)
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude\-class= class
Disable all effects (fades, rounded corners, shadows) for windows whose
WM_CLASS (res_name or res_class) matches
.IR class ,
case-insensitively. May be given multiple times. The window contents are
still composited normally.
.TP
.BI \-S
Enables synchronous operation.  Useful for debugging.
.SH BUGS
Bugs may be reported via the litecompmgr project's issue tracker.
